    "turn_text": "less now? Well, I think anyone who listened to that rally and what was coming out of it, it was clearly racist, it was clearly bigoted. And I know it was a comedian, at the same time he was not rebuked and initially by the campaign. No one came in and took the hook and said, pull him off the stage, have a think that someone had to know what he was going to say. He just don't put someone out on a rally like that with no understanding what he's going to be saying at all. It will have some effect. Maybe not necessarily New York City, which already can't. But you look at Allentown and Pennsylvania, we talked before about upstate, not so much upstate. In Rockland County, there's a fairly large pottery community. And I would just go back historically. There was another island, there was another island in the Atlantic Ocean, Ireland. The same thing happened to the Irish people. My forebears in this country, they became the target of rebuke. They were focused on, they said, people of garbage were coming from Ireland. You know, history is repeating itself. And it's unfortunate that we see this happening today that a whole people can be, go back to what the president, the former president did during the hurricane, throwing paper towels at people. You know, the disdain there for folks. And here, you know, these people can vote on the island for president. But you know what? Their children and their grandchildren can hear in the States. And I think that's something that's going to be played out.",
