    "turn_text": "Well, I think you saw something that the Trump campaign rarely does. And they put out a statement almost immediately after this came out. And I thought that told you everything you need to know about where they think this was not a helpful from them. Yeah, do I wish they had a different comedian there? Yeah, I sure. I think they wish they had a different comedian there, too. But look, This guilt by association, I don't think applies here. I mean, it wasn't Donald Trump who said it was everybody else who said it. Guilt by association doesn't, you typically work with these politicians, maybe for Kamala Harris, who was Joe Biden's vice president for the last four years. That may be held. But I think the problem for the Harris campaign and for Democrats here is that they spent the last several weeks as well engaging in dark rhetoric themselves using fascist language, comparing him to Hitler and all of this like. It takes away the sting and has less of a lead for them to stand on to go and criticize what happened last night. And if you look at the polls out this morning, I know we have a lot of discussions here every day about things that are set at Trump rallies or things he might have said. There are new rounds of polling out showing Trump up one in both Wisconsin and Pennsylvania and tied in Michigan. So it would seem to me the voters are kind of making up their minds at this juncture. Okay. I",
